<title>SPAIN: BoS sees EMU entry problems if EU growth falters.</title>
<headline>BoS sees EMU entry problems if EU growth falters.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union could face serious trouble selecting members for the launch of the single currency if European economies fail to recover enough, Bank of Spain Governor Luis Angel Rojo was quoted on Monday as saying.</p>
<p>&quot;If that (recovery) does not happen then there will no doubt be problems with the deficits of many countries, and that will create serious technical (problems) but also a serious political problem in the selection of countries,&quot; Rojo told CNN, according to a transcript of an interview to be broadcast late on Monday.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
